  "description": "You are Walt Disney. Your company makes 94.4 billion dollars a year. But first, you lost a rabbit.\n\nSources:\n- Wikipedia: Walt Disney: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walt_Disney\n- Wikipedia: Oswald the Lucky Rabbit: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oswald_the_Lucky_Rabbit\n- Wikipedia: Laugh-O-Gram Studio: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laugh-O-Gram_Studio\n- Wikipedia: The Walt Disney Company: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Walt_Disney_Company\n\nFrom the cited pages: Walt Disney moved to Hollywood in July 1923 at 21, after his Kansas City studio Laugh-O-Gram went bankrupt in 1923; he and Ub Iwerks created Oswald the Lucky Rabbit for distribution through Universal Pictures; in 1928 producer Charles Mintz cut the budget and hired away most of Disney's artists, and Disney found out Universal owned the rights to Oswald; to replace Oswald, Disney and Iwerks created Mickey Mouse in 1928, and Steamboat Willie, with synchronized sound, made Mickey popular; in February 2006 The Walt Disney Company got Oswald and 27 of Walt's Oswald shorts back from NBCUniversal in a trade that sent sportscaster Al Michaels from ABC/ESPN to NBC. The Walt Disney Company reported US$94.4 billion in revenue in fiscal 2025. Not financial advice.\n\n#shorts #disney #mickeymouse #howtheymakemoney",
